ssion digitalDoc soeg.kb.dk Session Queue-it-visitorsession audk.queue-it.net Session ahoy_unique_40035044 www.powr.io 12 hours _twpid .au.dk 1 year esctx-kueLUDLLq8k .login.microsoftonline.com Session device_self_generated_uuid .embion.au.dk 6 months esctx-jq5eySNoG0A .login.microsoftonline.com Session __Secure-typo3nonce_tB7LaxTdExn0Ueagy61Wzg law.medarbejdere.au.dk Session selvbetjening sbstads.au.dk Session X-SurveyIT-HAProxy-surveyxact_frontend survey.au.dk Session esctx-nfHdeloMxho .login.microsoftonline.com Session __Secure-ROLLOUT_TOKEN .youtube.com 5 months 4 weeks msal.cache.encryption forms.cloud.microsoft Session Queue-it-audk________________audkprod2026 audk.queue-it.net 1 day productCode soeg.kb.dk Session __Secure-UqZBpD3n3naPU20-9Fvn5i-TSO9FpchbYtbA9YCEpg3UXgo_ soeg.kb.dk 1 year esctx-O2uzNWDgQPY .login.microsoftonline.com Session esctx-cnOtbYn1wEE .login.microsoftonline.com Session What is a cookie? A cookie is a text file, that is stored on your computer, mobile or similar device. When visiting our website it is sent forth and back between your browser and a web server. It is used by AU or a third party, which is described more specific under the cookie descriptions at the bottom of this page. Cookies cannot contain malicious code such as virus. Cookies can be either temporary or permanent. The temporary cookies are linked to one specific visit, and are deleted again when you close the website. The permanent cookie is saved on your computer, mobile or tablet for a period of time. How long the various cookies remain is described in the cookie descriptions at the bottom of the page. Each time you visit the website, however, the cookie will be renewed and the period will thus start all over again. What data is collected via cookies? Most cookies collect anonymous data, such as the amount of time of your visit to the website, what pages you have visited, whether your computer, tablet or smartphone has used the pages before, which website you came from, which browser and operating system you use and the like. In some cases, IP addresses are also collected, which are personally identifiable data. Therefore, you can also read our Privacy Policy , which tells how we at AU process personal information. If any of the third party services, we use, process data on behalf of AU, we will, if possible, enter into a Data Processing Agreement with them. The supplier is thus not allowed to use the data for their own purposes or to pass them on to others. Delete cookies It is also possible to delete or block cookies. See the guide: https://www.allaboutcookies.org/manage-cookies/clear-cookies-installed.html The website is owned and published by: Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 DK-8000 Aarhus C Tel. no: 87 15 00 00 Email: au@au.dk Cookies consent ID : Cookie report created by CookieScript"
