    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-for-pfas-clear-and-swift-projects": {
      "title": "Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects",
      "description": "Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects Deadline 20 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology Frederiksborgvej 399 4000 Roskilde Fixed term part-time position 1 Nov 2026 - 31 Oct 2028 8 hours per week ID: 170639 Apply Are you passionate about environmental chemistry or mass spectrometry and can you contribute to the development of the project PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT? The Department of Environmental Science at Aarhus University is looking for one student assistant. Expected start date and duration of employment The position is from 1 November 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter, and for a period of 2 years. Job description You will be contributing to the organization of project datasets, digitalization and integration of data, and curation of research data and associated metadata. You will support harmonization of datasets, including data structures, variable names, units and metadata, and contribute to basic quality control and documentation. You will assist with data processing, tabulation and visualization when relevant. These activities will be carried out in close collaboration with researchers working in the PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects. Your profile Experience in handling and treating research datasets, environmental data and experimental metadata. Experience with SciexOS is an advantage. Experience with Excel and/or data handling in R or Python is an advantage. Be thorough and able to work independently and disciplined. Be able to communicate in English. Have an interest in environmental chemistry and data integration. The qualification requirement is enrolment at an institution of higher education. Who we are The Department of Environmental Science has about 150 employees working in basic and problem-oriented research within environmental science, including chemical and physical processes and interactions between environment and society. The department also carries out research-based consultancy for the public sector and provides research-based advice. The academic expertise ranges from atmospheric chemistry and physics, via environmental chemistry, microbiology and biotechnology to environmental economics, environmental geography, political science and sociology. The department is located in Roskilde, Denmark. This position will be based in the section for Environmental Chemistry and Toxicology. What we offer The department offers: high-quality research in a strong international network state-of-the-art research infrastructure, laboratories and access to shared equipment possibilities for scientific and personal development and career building an interdisciplinary environment with many national and international collaborators a research group with close working relationships and mutual support a climate encouraging lively, open and critical discussion within and across different fields of research Place of work and area of employment The place of work is Aarhus University, Department of Environmental Science, Frederiksborgvej 399, 4000 Roskilde, Denmark. Please note that the place of work is Roskilde, not Aarhus. Contact information For further information, please contact: Associate Professor Pedro Carvalho, +45 87 15 84 62, [email protected] Deadline Applications must be received no later than 20 October 2026. Formalities and salary range Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Union of Commercial and Clerical Employees in Denmark/State (HK/Stat) for clerical staff, laboratory technicians and IT employees and the joint collective agreement concluded between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Organisations of Public Employees - Denmark - Danish State Sector (the OAO-S joint collective agreement). Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Pedro Carvalho Associate Professor, Head of Section, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology +4587158462 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4522521469 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 20 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-at-the-center-for-hybrid-intelligence-chi-at-department-of-management": {
      "title": "Student Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant at the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI) at Department of Management - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Management Student Assistant at the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI) at Department of Management Deadline 21 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Department of Management Universitetsbyen 61 8000 Aarhus C Part-time position 12 hours per week ID: 170810 Apply The AI-first narrative promises speed and automation, but risks eroding human meaning and agency. At the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI), we believe in another path and that is combining human creativity, ethics and judgment with the scalability of AI. We are an interdisciplinary team of researchers and practitioners at the Department of Management, Aarhus BSS, Aarhus University. We develop frameworks and tools for human-AI collaboration, such as FERC and the 4P Framework, do a lot of workshops, exploring digital interfaces and we are behind the Hybrid Intelligence Manifesto, supported by over 900 signatories. Our websites are where all of this meets the world. We are looking for a creative and student assistant where your main task is to help us improve and develop our websites. The main website is made with Wordpress. As our student assistant, you will help shape how researchers, companies and the public experience hybrid intelligence. Our websites are one of the most important ways we share our activities on hybrid intelligence, where humans and AI meet to create meaningful innovation. As part of our team, you will work on live websites with real users and real impact. Your tasks Your tasks will include: Web design & maintenance: Designing, building and improving our websites so they are visually appealing, user-friendly and up to date. This is your main task. Improving structure, navigation and user experience across our sites. Graphic design: Creating visual material and graphics that fit our identity. Content: Publishing and updating content that communicates our projects, results and events to both academic and broader audiences. Ad hoc: We are a fast-moving team with many exciting projects, so you can expect a dynamic work environment with diverse tasks. We expect that you Have skills in web design. Knowledge or/and experience with WordPress Have an eye for aesthetics and UX. Be able to show examples of your work (a portfolio or a project is enough). Work in a structured and independent way. Have an interest in AI and technology Can communicate effectively, both in writing and verbally, in English and Danish. Nice to have: Experience in graphic design and image editing (e.g. Figma, Adobe or similar), Basic HTML/CSS You do not need to know everything above. Curiosity and a good eye for design matter more. What we offer Highly relevant practical experience for aspiring web designers, with your work visible to the public. Close collaboration with both students, professors, partners from different fields so you can grow your network and gain experience in AI. A young, interdisciplinary team that aims to create impact with our research, and a working environment characterised by respect, appreciation and collaboration. Who we are The Department of Management is part of Aarhus BSS , Aarhus University – a top 100 university. Aarhus BSS has achieved the triple-crown AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS accreditations. The department has an international research and teaching environment, employs approximately 160 Danish and international researchers, academic staff, and PhD students. We excel in business management, including strategy, innovation, marketing, organisation, digitalisation, and accounting. Our aim is to deliver high-quality research, with a strong emphasis on publishing in leading academic journals and presenting at recognised conferences. You can read more about the Department of Management at: http://mgmt.au.dk . Contact information For further information about the position, please contact Rigmor Lyck by phone at 2479 6701 or by [email protected] If you need assistance uploading your application or have questions regarding the recruitment process, please contact HR-Coordinator Line Greve Brunhøi at: [email protected] . Practical information The average working time is approximately 12 hours per week, and the place of work is Universitetsbyen 614, 8000 Aarhus C. Applications must be submitted electronically and received no later than 21 October 2026. The expected starting date is 1 November 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. Please submit a short, motivated application and your CV, including information about your degree programme and current semester. Terms of employment You will be employed as an hourly-paid student assistant under the collective agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Organisations of Public Employees – Denmark (OAO-S Collective Agreement, State Sector), as well as the organisational agreement for clerical employees, laboratory technicians and IT staff (HK). Aarhus University Aarhus University is an academically diverse and research-intensive university with a strong commitment to high-quality research and education and the development of society nationally and globally. The university offers an inspiring research and teaching environment to its 37,000 students (FTEs) and 8,700 employees and has an annual revenue of EUR 1.106 billion. Learn more at www.international.au.dk/ Questions about the position\n                            ? Jacob Sherson Associate Professor, Department of Management +4528775765 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4587150584 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 21 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
